g_xl="""<h2>How to convert a PDF to Excel</h2><ol><li>Choose a PDF with real text, such as a bank statement, an invoice or a report exported from software.</li><li>Choose <b>All pages in one sheet</b> for one long table (repeated header rows on later pages are removed), or <b>One sheet per page</b>.</li><li>Click <b>Convert to Excel</b> and download the .xlsx file, or a CSV file that opens correctly in Excel.</li></ol>
<h2>How it works</h2><p>The tool reads the position of every piece of text on each page with Mozilla's pdf.js. Text at the same height becomes a row, and the left and right edges of the text are grouped into columns, so amounts stay in the right column even when a title spans several columns (that title becomes a merged cell). Each cell is then typed:</p><ul><li><b>Amounts become numbers</b> you can add up: <code>1.234.567,89</code>, <code>1,234,567.89</code>, <code>-1.500</code>, <code>(1.500)</code>, <code>12%</code> and <code>₫1.000</code> are all read correctly. A single dot or comma followed by exactly three digits is read as a thousands separator.</li><li><b>Codes stay text:</b> phone numbers like <code>0912345678</code>, codes like <code>00123</code> and long account numbers keep their leading zeros and all their digits.</li><li><b>Dates stay text</b> exactly as printed, such as <code>04/11/2026</code>, so day and month are never swapped.</li></ul>
<h2>Tips</h2><ul><li>Scanned PDFs (photos of paper) have no text layer and are not supported here. Use <a href='/image-to-text/'>Image to Text</a> instead.</li><li>For a bank statement, check the totals: add up the debit and credit columns in Excel and compare them with the totals on the PDF.</li><li>The CSV files are UTF-8 with a byte-order mark, so Vietnamese and other accented text opens correctly in Excel.</li></ul>"""+FAQ2(("Is my PDF uploaded?","No. The PDF is read and the Excel file is created on your own device. Your bank statements and invoices never leave your browser."),("Why are some numbers stored as text?","Values with leading zeros, more than 15 digits, or dates are kept as text on purpose, so phone numbers, account numbers and dates are not changed."),("Can I convert a scanned PDF?","No. A scanned PDF only contains pictures. Use Image to Text (OCR) to get its text first."),("Can I convert a password-protected PDF?","Remove the password first with <a href='/unlock-pdf/'>Unlock PDF</a>, then convert the copy."),("Does it work with large files?","Yes. Progress is shown page by page; a 100-page statement usually takes well under a minute."))
add2("pdf-to-excel","PDF tools","PDF to Excel Converter","PDF to Excel – Convert PDF Tables to XLSX & CSV Free, No Upload","Convert PDF tables and bank statements to Excel (.xlsx) or CSV on your device. Amounts become real numbers; leading zeros and dates are kept. Free, nothing uploaded.",ui_xl,js_xl,g_xl)
